HTTP Server:- 
Step-1:- We have to import http module either by using require() or import statement.

const http = require('http')

-The http module provides methods to create and manage servers.

Step-2:- Create server by using createServer()

const server = http.createServer((req,res)=>{
		res.writeHead(200, {'Content-Type': 'text/plain'});
		res.end("message");
});

req -> Request object which contains data from client side
res -> Response object which is used to send data to client
writeHead() -> it is a method which is used to define the header or set the status code and Content type.
end() -> It is a method, which is used to send data to client side.

Step-3:- Listen/Start the server by using listen()
-We need to pass a port number as an argument to the listen() to run the server on a specific port.

server.listen(3000, ()=>{
	log("Server runing at http://localhost:3000")
})

-Port number can be anything in between 1024 and 65535(e.g: 3000, 5000, 8000)
-Now we can open our browser and go to the URL to see the response.

#Important Request Properties:-
req.url :- the path requested by client side 
e.g: /about , /contact

req.methods :- It is the HTTP method used to check request type
e.g: GET, POST, PUT

req.headers :- It contains all request headers
e.g: {host: 'localhost...'

#Important Response Properties:-
res.writeHead(statusCode, header) :- Is is used to set the HTTP status code and response header.

res.write(data) :- It is used to send data in Chunks

res.end([data]) :- Sends response, and it must be called

200 -> OK -> Request successful
201 -> Created -> Data created
400 -> Bad Request -> Invalid Request
401 -> Unauthorized -> No authentication
403 -> Forbidden -> Access denied
404 -> Not found -> Page not found
500 -> Internal server error -> Server crashed


Step-1: initialize Project
Open terminal and run the command to initialize npm
-> npm init -y

Step-2: Install Express
Install Express via npm
-> npm install express

Step-3: Create Server File
Create a file named index.js or server.js as mentioned in your pacakage.json file.
The file should be present in root directory of the project.

Step-4: Import express module and initialize the express.
const express =  require('express')
const app = express()

Step-5: Define a port and start/listen the server
const PORT = 8000

app.listen(PORT, ()=>{
		log("Server running")
	});
	

res.send(), res.json(), res.status()...
app.get("/", (req, res) => {

  res.send("This is an example of response");
  console.log(req.method);
});



app.get("/books", (req, res) => {
  res.send("Normal route");
});

app.get("/books/:id", (req, res) => {
  res.send("Parameterized route");
});

app.get("/books/:id", (req, res) => {

  res.send(`Parameterized route ${req.params.id}`);
});


